A||||5||Jaei Sun||Alternative Front Battery Mount without Cutting||||4||
Z||000000||Jaei Sun||02-08-2001||12:57 AM||||I'm all for moving the battery to the front compartment to get the weight xfer benefits, but the only thing I'm not for is cutting the front trunk up and installing a (potentially expensive) battery tray.  I was wondering if anyone has tried one of the Holley Annihilator Batteries?  If you take the spare tire and flip it around and place this battery in the gap it possibly might work.  The dimensions of this battery are: <BR>Height: 6 13/16" x Length: 9 3/4" x Width: 5 3/16".  The typical cost of the battery box I've found was $50-120, and if you get a Optima sealed batt. that's $140 (red top) and $180 (yellow).  It's around $180 for the Annihilator Batt.<P>I moved the battery that was in the Fiero (1 year old) to my other car, and I want to get a High Quality Battery and this might be the solution.<P>More info about the batt. here:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.weiand.com/HiOctn/ProdLine/AV/IS/ISA/880-100.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.weiand.com/HiOctn/ProdLine/AV/IS/ISA/880-100.html</A>  <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://members.aol.com/umebottle3/fie_sig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Jaei Sun (edited 02-08-2001).]||||reg||4
Z||000001||KEV||02-08-2001||07:07 AM||||I CAN SET YOU UP WITH A OPYIMA BATTERY MUCH CHEAPER AND A BATTERY TRAY FOR THE FRONT. BYE THE WAY WOULD YOU LIKE TO JOIN THE MINN FIERO CLUB I'M THE EVENTS CHAIRMEN FOR THE CLUB. LET ME KNOW.  KEVIN ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||02-08-2001||07:27 AM||||optima now has a smaller size red top for $119 at interstate batteries.  I was able to <BR>fit it in the stock location, still using the plastic side to the battery tray.  The regular optima would not fit, without taking the side tray away.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005058.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/005058.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||danny boy||02-08-2001||10:15 PM|||| If your car does not have A/C, you dont have to cut anything. On my late '86 coupe I ran the cables along the gas tank and thru the opening for the A/C lines. the battery tray was out of a '75 chevy truck. I didnt cut anything, just drilled the holes for the tray to mount.||||reg||1
